// `deep` gets a read-only browser (issue #15, 2026-11-22): some Slovak shops load prices and
// shipping with JavaScript, so `web_fetch` sees none. jorah-guard (lib/policy.js) lets a consult
// agent use only open, navigate, snapshot, text, screenshot, tabs, focus, close, status and start,
// in Jorah's own headless profile in its sandbox: no act (click, type, select), emulate, requests,
// signed-in or host profiles, nodes or dashboards. Page JavaScript evaluation stays off for every
// agent (p5-fixes.patch.json5, browser.evaluateEnabled false).
//
// Apply only on Adam's yes, after the guard change is deployed (the guard must come first, or
// deep's browser would get main's rules, which let it click). The live list is read and "browser"
// appended, the way scripts/pc/install-errands.sh does for price_compare; never replace the list.
//   openclaw --profile jorah config get agents.entries.deep.tools.sandbox.tools.alsoAllow
//   (append "browser", then config set with the full list)
// Undo: config set the list without "browser".
{
  agents: {
    entries: {
      deep: {
        tools: { sandbox: { tools: { alsoAllow: ["<the live list>", "browser"] } } },
      },
    },
  },
}
